  "insights": [
    "Behaviour alone was enough to recover the hidden motives. From 208,000 observed decisions the learner matched the true reward weights with cosine 0.9999 (largest error 0.008, on status gain). With a single episode (1,300 decisions) the cosine was already 0.999.",
    "Who an agent listens to matters as much as what they want. Recovered attention named the true influencer in 98% of held-out decisions, against 54% for the most similar neighbour and 26% for a random one.",
    "Supervision +0.2 cut the final bad share most, by 0.243 (from 0.73), and its 95% interval excludes zero. The real wave 4 network changed it by -0.001. Removing any single tie moved it by at most 0.007, so in this model behaviour is driven by incentives and supervision more than by any one relationship.",
    "A model of motives generalises better than a copy of actions: rolled forward, the recovered reward stays closer to the true cascade than behavioural cloning (mean gap 0.004 vs 0.012). One-step accuracy alone hides this: 0.46 for the recovered reward vs 0.43 for cloning."
  ],
